Package: mlr3HTE
Title: Metalearner Learners for Heterogeneous Treatment Effects in mlr3
Version: 0.23
Author: Flexible Pangzi <zhangkaicr@foxmail.com> [cre, aut]
Maintainer: Flexible Pangzi <zhangkaicr@foxmail.com>
Description: A small, mlr3-native R package that implements the S-, T-, X-, R- and DR-learners
    for conditional average treatment effect (CATE) estimation. The same engine covers
    continuous, binary and survival outcomes and handles both randomized (RCT) and
    observational data (via internal propensity-score IPTW or user-supplied weights).
    Survival outcomes are supported natively via 'survival' and 'ranger'
    (no 'mlr3proba' dependency). It ships both a functional API and a parametric
    mlr3 Learner subclass that plugs into resample()/benchmark()/tune().
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
